{"type": "root", "attrs": {"index": "no"}, "body": [{"level": 0, "type": "title", "indent": 0, "text": ["Pyro Configure Color Smoke"], "extent": [12, 43]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Overview"], "extent": [43, 59], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["There are several Pyro Configure examples available through the ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/basics/tabmenu", "type": "link", "text": ["tab menu"], "fullpath": "/basics/tabmenu.html"}, ". These are similar to ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/shelf/index", "type": "link", "text": ["shelf tools"], "fullpath": "/shelf/index.html"}, " that put down networks of nodes for learning purposes. The ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Pyro\nConfigure Colored Smoke"]}, " example illustrates 3 colored smokes interacting. It also demonstrates how to use the feedback wires to add additional fields to the simulation."], "extent": [59, 438]}, {"type": "video_group", "body": [{"ext": null, "type": "video", "indent": 0, "role": "item", "extent": [438, 446], "body": [], "container": true, "attrs": {"src": "/videos/pyro/coppyro/ColorSmoke.webm"}}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Important nodes"], "extent": [494, 516], "body": [{"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["SOURCE"]}], "extent": [516, 527], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Wire a Mono layer into this to adjust where the smoke emits from.  A value of ", {"type": "code", "text": ["0"]}, " will have no fire and ", {"type": "code", "text": ["1"]}, " will have the full thickness."], "extent": [527, 670]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["COLOR"]}], "extent": [670, 679], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Wire an RGB layer into this to set the color of newly emitted smoke."], "extent": [679, 753]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["pyro_configure1"]}], "extent": [753, 772], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Adjust the resolution of the smoke.  This is the number of voxels across the default imaging window.  Higher resolutions will take considerably more time and memory."], "extent": [772, 943]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["layertovdbleafpoints6"]}, ", ", {"type": "code", "text": ["pyro_sourcefromlayer10"]}], "extent": [943, 994], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The VDB has to be activated so you can source into it.  ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop/layertovdbleafpoints", "type": "link", "text": ["Layer to VDB Leaf Points"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop/layertovdbleafpoints.html"}, " handles the activation from the ", {"type": "code", "text": ["SOURCE"]}, " layer, while the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop/pyro_sourcefromlayer", "type": "link", "text": ["Pyro Source from Layer"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop/pyro_sourcefromlayer.html"}, " handles the actual sourcing.  The thickness and inputs for these two nodes should match."], "extent": [994, 1314]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["pyro_block_begin6"]}], "extent": [1314, 1335], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The start of the simulation loop.  All nodes inside the convex hull (highlighted area) will run every simulation step. The simulation is clipped from ", {"type": "code", "text": ["-1"]}, " to ", {"type": "code", "text": ["1"]}, " by default, and can be controlled by modifying the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Clip X/Y/Z"]}, " parameters."], "extent": [1335, 1580]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The ", {"type": "code", "text": ["feedback"]}, " input port is only read on the first frame of the simulation.  After that, the ", {"type": "code", "text": ["feedback"]}, " output port will contain what was passed into the ", {"type": "code", "text": ["feedback"]}, " input port of ", {"type": "code", "text": ["pyro_block_end6"]}, " on the previous frame.  Note that the ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/copernicus/cables", "type": "link", "text": ["cable structure"], "fullpath": "/copernicus/cables.html"}, " must be the same. The types and names of the wires must not change."], "extent": [1580, 1926]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["All feedback wires that match the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["VDBs to Activate"]}, " pattern will be activated for new sources, and all feedback wires that match the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["VDBs to Advect"]}, " will be advected by velocity.  These both are the default ", {"type": "code", "text": ["*"]}, ", so the VDBs passed through named ", {"type": "code", "text": ["Cd"]}, " and ", {"type": "code", "text": ["Cd_weight"]}, " will be resized and advected.  Note this pattern is also used to decide if the default ", {"type": "code", "text": ["density"]}, " and ", {"type": "code", "text": ["temperature"]}, " VDBs will be updated."], "extent": [1926, 2340]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["extra_Cd_fields"]}, ", ", {"type": "code", "text": ["cableunpack3"]}, ", ", {"type": "code", "text": ["cablepack2"]}], "extent": [2340, 2389], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["To properly simulate color, two VDBs are needed. One is a vector VDB of the pre-multiplied color, the other is a scalar VDB of the amount of color present. These nodes combine these two VDBs into a ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/copernicus/cables", "type": "link", "text": ["cable"], "fullpath": "/copernicus/cables.html"}, ", extract them, and ensure they are named the same so the feedback is consistent."], "extent": [2389, 2700]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["inward_velocity"]}], "extent": [2700, 2719], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Takes a 2d velocity field that points inward generated by the previous nodes and projects it onto\n    the VDB to create a 3d inward pointed velocity field."], "extent": [2719, 2880]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["pyro_buoyancy6"]}], "extent": [2880, 2898], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Instead of having hot air move upwards, the direction of buoyancy is controlled by the ", {"type": "code", "text": ["direction"]}, " input.  The smoke in this simulation rises to the center of the layer."], "extent": [2898, 3073]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["vdbfromlayer1"]}], "extent": [3073, 3090], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Transfers the colors of the ", {"type": "code", "text": ["COLOR"]}, " layer to a VDB by projecting the layer onto the VDB."], "extent": [3090, 3184]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["add7"]}, ", ", {"type": "code", "text": ["multiply1"]}, ", ", {"type": "code", "text": ["add8"]}], "extent": [3184, 3213], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Perform a weighted sum of the previous ", {"type": "code", "text": ["Cd"]}, " and ", {"type": "code", "text": ["Cd_weight"]}, " with the newly sourced values."], "extent": [3213, 3309]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["pyro_lightambient6"]}], "extent": [3309, 3331], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Computes lighting for the fire\u2019s smoke using an ambient light source. Increasing smoke density (with the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Density Scale"]}, " parameter) increases the contrast of self-shadows."], "extent": [3331, 3510]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["pyro_lightfrompoints1"]}], "extent": [3510, 3535], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Computes lighting from the top left of the smoke, providing directional shadows."], "extent": [3535, 3621]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["regularize"]}], "extent": [3621, 3638], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Color weights close to zero can generate NANs or Infinity when divided out. You can avoid this by boosting the weight slightly."], "extent": [3638, 3771]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["normalize"]}], "extent": [3771, 3784], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Un-premultiply the color by dividing by the color weight. This provides the absolute color of the smoke."], "extent": [3784, 3894]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["mix_in_color"]}], "extent": [3894, 3910], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The light field from the lighting nodes is multiplied by the smoke color to get the effective color of the smoke."], "extent": [3910, 4029]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "code", "text": ["rasterizevolume6"]}], "extent": [4029, 4049], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Renders the flame into a layer.  The ", {"type": "code", "text": ["camera_ref"]}, " can use an imported camera from the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop/cameraimport", "type": "link", "text": ["Camera Import COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop/cameraimport.html"}, " to change the view or resolution of the render."], "extent": [4049, 4230]}], "container": true}], "container": true}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Learning from this example"], "extent": [4230, 4263], "body": [{"type": "task_group", "body": [{"ext": null, "type": "task", "indent": 0, "text": [" Change what colors are used"], "role": "item", "extent": [4263, 4300], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Change the input of the ", {"type": "code", "text": ["COLOR"]}, " node."], "extent": [4300, 4343]}], "container": true}, {"ext": null, "type": "task", "indent": 0, "text": [" Create different smoke sources"], "role": "item", "extent": [4343, 4382], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Change the input of ", {"type": "code", "text": ["SOURCE"]}, "."], "extent": [4382, 4417]}], "container": true}, {"ext": null, "type": "task", "indent": 0, "text": [" Control the amount of smoke emitted"], "role": "item", "extent": [4417, 4461], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Change or animate the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Brightness"]}, " parameter on the ", {"type": "code", "text": ["bright2"]}, " node to control how much smoke is created."], "extent": [4461, 4573]}], "container": true}, {"ext": null, "type": "task", "indent": 0, "text": [" Create other 2d patterns for the smoke to rise along"], "role": "item", "extent": [4573, 4634], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Change the input of ", {"type": "code", "text": ["inward_velocity"]}, "."], "extent": [4634, 4676]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}]}], "title": ["Pyro Configure Color Smoke"]}